(6364702, 942189, 125659, '<td valign="top">Fore to the forehead? lol. great idea</td>', 'Fore to the forehead? lol. great idea', '2011-03-27 23:16:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6364704, 941937, 125659, '<td valign="top">awesome photo!</td>', 'awesome photo!', '2011-03-27 23:19:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6364705, 941948, 125659, '<td valign="top">good photo. I would personally like it more if it was in sharper focus.</td>', 'good photo. I would personally like it more if it was in sharper focus.', '2011-03-27 23:25:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6364707, 942209, 125659, '<td valign="top">cool photo. great composition.</td>', 'cool photo. great composition.', '2011-03-27 23:26:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365057, 942244, 93565, '<td valign="top">I like this shot, it''s really got a pleasant mix of elements. But, I''m left feeling like the focal point is subverted by the composition. The overwhelmingly bright mountains and sky pull the viewer there instinctively, and the lines of the field pull us away from your subject as well. To me, very few things bring us toward the person, with their relative darkness (their white is subdued, the colors are darker and, though nicely saturated, are not particularly bright or eye catching to me).</td>', 'I like this shot, it''s really got a pleasant mix of elements. But, I''m left feeling like the focal point is subverted by the composition. The overwhelmingly bright mountains and sky pull the viewer there instinctively, and the lines of the field pull us away from your subject as well. To me, very few things bring us toward the person, with their relative darkness (their white is subdued, the colors are darker and, though nicely saturated, are not particularly bright or eye catching to me).', '2011-03-28 04:41:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365064, 942113, 93565, '<td valign="top">In portraits, it''s typical that the attention of the viewer should be focused upon the person depicted. Here your subject has been subverted by the hat in numerous ways. It is brighter, more vibrant, and his eyes are somewhat shaded/shielded by the hat as well.</td>', 'In portraits, it''s typical that the attention of the viewer should be focused upon the person depicted. Here your subject has been subverted by the hat in numerous ways. It is brighter, more vibrant, and his eyes are somewhat shaded/shielded by the hat as well.', '2011-03-28 04:45:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365065, 942252, 93565, '<td valign="top">Great shot of a great blue heron, but the scene and composition do little to focus the viewer. Quite a bit of the scene is cluttered by other elements and compete for my attention. The light colored rocks, the road in the back, the branches in the foreground, trees in the back.. they all vie for attention. A decreased depth of field would have done MUCH to help this.</td>', 'Great shot of a great blue heron, but the scene and composition do little to focus the viewer. Quite a bit of the scene is cluttered by other elements and compete for my attention. The light colored rocks, the road in the back, the branches in the foreground, trees in the back.. they all vie for attention. A decreased depth of field would have done MUCH to help this.', '2011-03-28 04:48:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365066, 942314, 93565, '<td valign="top">Very different take on things. I like this... sorta otherwordly, but nice.</td>', 'Very different take on things. I like this... sorta otherwordly, but nice.', '2011-03-28 04:49:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365070, 942185, 93565, '<td valign="top">Surprisingly clean image considering you must have been cranking the ISO to keep your shutter duration short enough to keep your stars from trailing. Cool scene.</td>', 'Surprisingly clean image considering you must have been cranking the ISO to keep your shutter duration short enough to keep your stars from trailing. Cool scene.', '2011-03-28 04:52:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365073, 942032, 93565, '<td valign="top">The blossoms command my attention too much, seemingly contrary to your title.</td>', 'The blossoms command my attention too much, seemingly contrary to your title.', '2011-03-28 04:54:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365074, 941966, 93565, '<td valign="top">I''m pretty sure this locale has been used a good deal before. In any case, I liked it then, and I like it now. Radiating lines, plus the windows and shadows... all of them lead us up. The yellow sign adds a bit of a counterpoint, bringing us to the bottom, but always to return upwards, drawn.</td>', 'I''m pretty sure this locale has been used a good deal before. In any case, I liked it then, and I like it now. Radiating lines, plus the windows and shadows... all of them lead us up. The yellow sign adds a bit of a counterpoint, bringing us to the bottom, but always to return upwards, drawn.', '2011-03-28 04:56:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365078, 941977, 93565, '<td valign="top">I certainly like the idea of this. The strength of what is really the most insignificant part of the landscape, commanding the rest and the viewer too... nice usage.</td>', 'I certainly like the idea of this. The strength of what is really the most insignificant part of the landscape, commanding the rest and the viewer too... nice usage.', '2011-03-28 05:03:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365079, 941336, 93565, '<td valign="top">I feel a DQ coming on, and I think that vignette is a strong part of what centers us on the engine, too. The tree is too divergent from the subject for me.</td>', 'I feel a DQ coming on, and I think that vignette is a strong part of what centers us on the engine, too. The tree is too divergent from the subject for me.', '2011-03-28 05:04:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365081, 941959, 93565, '<td valign="top">I don''t personally feel as though this embodies the challenge well. There are many items competing for my attention, nothing holding it sufficiently.</td>', 'I don''t personally feel as though this embodies the challenge well. There are many items competing for my attention, nothing holding it sufficiently.', '2011-03-28 05:06:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365082, 941205, 93565, '<td valign="top">I''m of the opinion that a photo should say everything in and of itself, and any insufficiency in this regard should be seen as a detraction.<br/>The lighting feels a little flat, and the arrows have the perverse effect of pulling me away from the model due to their brightness and placement instead of directing me towards her.</td>', 'I''m of the opinion that a photo should say everything in and of itself, and any insufficiency in this regard should be seen as a detraction.The lighting feels a little flat, and the arrows have the perverse effect of pulling me away from the model due to their brightness and placement instead of directing me towards her.', '2011-03-28 05:12:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365097, 941733, 93565, '<td valign="top">Best moon shot I''ve seen in the challenge so far, and probably will end up being overall. I''m biased towards areas bereft of...well... everything, but this is just a great use of openness. I love how despite the small size of the moon, and the vastness of the scene, I am still perfectly directed. Very nice, great job.</td>', 'Best moon shot I''ve seen in the challenge so far, and probably will end up being overall. I''m biased towards areas bereft of...well... everything, but this is just a great use of openness. I love how despite the small size of the moon, and the vastness of the scene, I am still perfectly directed. Very nice, great job.', '2011-03-28 05:49:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365255, 942218, 129697, '<td valign="top">i like it. the worst, its true. but damn it is good :)</td>', 'i like it. the worst, its true. but damn it is good :)', '2011-03-28 10:25:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365264, 942142, 129697, '<td valign="top">good colors, and sharp<br/>well done:)</td>', 'good colors, and sharpwell done:)', '2011-03-28 10:29:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365334, 941045, 129697, '<td valign="top">spookey, and misteryous.</td>', 'spookey, and misteryous.', '2011-03-28 10:49:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365344, 941873, 129697, '<td valign="top">really good picture. amazing:)</td>', 'really good picture. amazing:)', '2011-03-28 11:06:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365454, 941368, 130456, '<td valign="top">Loveee this picture :)</td>', 'Loveee this picture :)', '2011-03-28 13:32:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6365488, 941650, 117474, '<td valign="top">It''s a great shot. And I''m gonna score it high because I can''t fault anything on it, but I don''t think I like it much. <br/> <br/>To me the tones, darks, split in green to brown, position of the baby... they all suggest sadness and a sense of mortality, or sickness or morbidity to me. Tones and darks--classic portrayal of this. The shift from green on the left to brown on the right--symbolises crossing from life to death to me. The position of the baby makes me think it fell from the tree, that it''s very still, and perhaps dead :( The mushroom (least I think it''s a mushroom) by his left foot is a fungus, which is something that suggests death to me too, for some reason, reinforcing the theme stronger. And the blurredness of the brown area conveys uncertainty about the afterlife. <br/>In all these ways I can''t stop staring at the shot. So it''s an excellent image for the challenge--the child is the focus, but the background, tones, colours, slight desaturation... they all support it magnificently. It''s incredibly captivating, deep and thought provoking shot. But I don''t like it because, well, nobody likes thinking of dying babies to be fair. I don''t know if I''m making sense here, but it''s getting a 9 from me. Maybe a 10... I''ll think about it before rollover. I get so much from it. And that''d mean it''ll get a favourite from me... which is odd in an image I don''t like, eh? :)<br/>Though perhaps I''m reading too much into it. <br/> <br/>Best of luck with it! Such a provoking image is rare to see here, I think.</td>', 'It''s a great shot. And I''m gonna score it high because I can''t fault anything on it, but I don''t think I like it much.  To me the tones, darks, split in green to brown, position of the baby... they all suggest sadness and a sense of mortality, or sickness or morbidity to me. Tones and darks--classic portrayal of this. The shift from green on the left to brown on the right--symbolises crossing from life to death to me. The position of the baby makes me think it fell from the tree, that it''s very still, and perhaps dead :( The mushroom (least I think it''s a mushroom) by his left foot is a fungus, which is something that suggests death to me too, for some reason, reinforcing the theme stronger. And the blurredness of the brown area conveys uncertainty about the afterlife. In all these ways I can''t stop staring at the shot. So it''s an excellent image for the challenge--the child is the focus, but the background, tones, colours, slight desaturation... they all support it magnificently. It''s incredibly captivating, deep and thought provoking shot. But I don''t like it because, well, nobody likes thinking of dying babies to be fair. I don''t know if I''m making sense here, but it''s getting a 9 from me. Maybe a 10... I''ll think about it before rollover. I get so much from it. And that''d mean it''ll get a favourite from me... which is odd in an image I don''t like, eh? :)Though perhaps I''m reading too much into it.  Best of luck with it! Such a provoking image is rare to see here, I think.', '2011-03-28 14:19:38.000000', NULL, 1),
